course: dictionary
lesson: 4286
title: Science words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Science words often come with clues in the sentence. «Owen's football smashed Mr Patel's greenhouse in Leeds.» A greenhouse is something a ball can smash, so it must be a building with breakable glass in it. Context tells you what kind of thing it is before you check the dictionary.
explain: A greenhouse is a building made mostly of glass or clear plastic where plants are grown because it stays warm inside. «A greenhouse keeps plants warm so crops can grow in cold seasons.» The clue is in the words cold seasons: the plants need the warmth inside the glass to grow when outside is cold.
explain: The word greenhouse is also used in other phrases, like greenhouse effect and greenhouse gases. «A greenhouse stays warm in the same way as a parked car: light gets in easily, but the warmth cannot escape well.» The car comparison helps you picture the idea, and it is the key to understanding the greenhouse effect.
fact: A greenhouse is a building made mostly of glass or clear plastic, used to grow plants.
fact: The greenhouse effect is the way some gases in the air trap the sun's heat and keep the Earth warm.
fact: Carbon dioxide and methane are greenhouse gases, and they trap heat.
fact: More greenhouse gases in the air means the planet gets warmer.
fact: Without the greenhouse effect, Earth would average about minus 18 degrees Celsius, which is too cold for most life.
exercise: «A greenhouse keeps plants warm so crops can grow in cold seasons.» What is a greenhouse for? | Storing bicycles | Cooking food over a fire | *Keeping plants warm so they can grow | Keeping cars cool in the summer
exercise: «Owen's football smashed Mr Patel's greenhouse in Leeds.» What does smashed tell you about the greenhouse? | *It was broken into many pieces | It was painted bright blue | It was too small to see | It was broken
exercise: «Gases such as carbon dioxide and methane trap some of the heat Earth gives off.» Find and copy one word that means catch and hold. | planet | heat | gases | *trap
test: Which of these is a greenhouse gas? | Sand | Sunlight | *Methane | Glass
test: What does the greenhouse effect describe? | The way glass breaks in the sun | *The way some gases in the air trap the sun's heat and keep Earth warm | The way cars park in the shade | The way plants grow faster in the dark
exam: Why does a greenhouse stay warm, like a parked car? | It is painted black inside | *Light gets in easily, but the warmth cannot escape well | It has a fire burning inside | Plants give out ice
